# Keep the files that are embedded into the binary at compile time -- and the
# Rust sources checked by `cargo fmt` -- in LF on every platform.
#
# The Jinja templates and the static `typed-fetch.ts` asset are read from disk
# by `build.rs` / `include_str!`, and the generated TypeScript must be
# byte-identical regardless of the checkout. A Windows checkout (core.autocrlf)
# would otherwise embed CRLF into those files. `cargo fmt --check` likewise
# expects LF.
*.jinja text eol=lf
*.ts text eol=lf
*.rs text eol=lf
